## Industry facts from Strategic Graphs (Q3) — approximate, chart-read

- **OC ranking:** SpaceBikes 30 · MILC 24 · Bike Bros/LiteCycle/BB LLC 15 · Spoke'd Up 14 · **WeBike 8 (LAST)**. Only firm that *reduced* OC.
- **Fixed capacity:** SpaceBikes 32 · WeBike/MILC 24 · rest 16. We own the 2nd-most and used the least.
- **Under-scheduling raised unit cost:** labor/unit **$130 → $205**, COGS/unit **~$520 → ~$620**, utilization 16% → 73%. Right-sizing OC cuts cost *and* ends stock-outs.
- **Productivity is mid-pack, NOT behind:** industry 68–73%; ours 72% prod / 70% sales. Pay is low-middle (prod $20,757 in a $20.5–23.5k range; sales $24,425 in $22–27k). **The error was planning on 85% — plan 73–75%.**
- **Marketing is fine:** ads 19 (2nd), spend $119k (3rd), price ~$1,400 (3rd), Marketing Effectiveness at par. Weak spots: organic SEM clicks ~150 vs 440 best; **store+web spend $121k = LOWEST in industry**.
- **Leakage:** share of demand **9.6%** vs share of units sold **7.3%**. Demand growth +235% = highest in industry. We create demand well and fill it badly.
- **Demand per head is LAST:** ~45/SP vs 60 typical, 72 best (store 46 vs 88; web 42 vs 95) — headcount is at parity (14), output per head is not.
- **Segments:** Speed **2,878** (all 7 firms, our 7.5%) · Recreation **2,060** (most searches ~1,350, our 2.6%) · Mountain **1,621** (smallest/slowest, BB LLC 46.3%, our 22.1%).
- **BB LLC** = leader: all 3 segments, *highest* price ~$1,480, most ads (24), Asset Mgmt 0.920, fixed cap only 16 + ~7 OT (buys flexibility, not printers).
- **SpaceBikes** = cumulative leader: skips Mountain, Rec 34.5% + Speed 20.4%, fixed cap 32.
- **Bike Bros** = cautionary tale: 1 store, 0 web centers, 7 SP, share falling everywhere. Don't cut channel.
- **Stores:** everyone but Bike Bros has 2 → **city #3 is a real differentiator**.

## Brand judgment (Q3 actual — exact from report)

- **Hike Bike 56/73/1 — Mountain 73 is TIED FOR BEST IN INDUSTRY** (with Bike Bros TERRAMAX + BB LLC Blu Ruged Ballz). **Ceiling is 73; do NOT redesign.**
- Key proof: BB LLC has an **identical 56/73/1** design and **46.3%** Mountain share vs our **22.1%**. Same product, 2.1x share → gap is **supply + coverage + ad volume, not product**.
- **Swift Bike 10/1/72 — 2nd WORST Speed brand.** Ceiling 77 (MACH I.I, LiteSpeed Pro+ at 12/1/77). 8 of 9 rival Speed brands beat us. Profile is close → modest redesign closes most of the gap.
- Speed ceiling **77**, Mountain **73**, Recreation **76** (MountainCruise1). Nobody exceeds these.
- **Designs are commoditising** — many firms share byte-identical profiles (56/73/1 ×3, 12/1/77 ×2, 9/1/76 ×3, 7/1/74 ×2, 73/1/1 ×2). No one wins on product alone.
- **Brand count ≠ share:** Bike Bros 5 brands → 7.5% (last); SpaceBikes 2 brands → 19.8% (cumulative leader). We have 2. **A 3rd brand is not a Q4 priority.**
- Recreation spillover: Hike Bike scores **56** with Rec buyers and pulled **54 untargeted units**; dedicated Rec brands score 73–76, so spillover can't win. Park for Q5.

## Q4 standing priorities

1. Schedule OC **to the forecast** (≈13/day required, **15/day suggested**; fixed 24 is enough — no printers needed)
2. Raise compensation toward upper quartile (sales ~$26.5k, prod ~$22.5k) but **budget 74% productivity, never 85%**
3. Stop issuing stock while ~$1M sits idle; deploy cash into revenue (city #3, people, ads)
4. **Do not cut channel spend** — it's already the industry's lowest; re-staff web
5. **Speed: fix, don't abandon.** Redesign Swift Bike toward 12/1/77 + strengthen the Speed ad (judgment 70)
6. **Leave Hike Bike's design alone** — spend on supplying and selling it instead

